KG42.register("nodes-fc739c63e397a250d8d9ca93",{"id":"KG40-80b56ab23344a0b7","code":"BID014.2","label":"Multi-carrier supply quantity and valuation submission","definition":"The supplier submits the supply quantity and unit valuation according to the energy-carrying commodity identifier, forming an energy-commodity auction input not limited to electricity.","layer":"L3","template_code":"DA","concept_id":"bidding.supply","concept_ids":["bidding.supply"],"identity_dimensions":{"identity_fields":["Submitter: energy-commodity supplier","Object: supply quantity and valuation identified by energy-carrying variety","Function: provide supply-side clearing input for the commodity"]},"exclusions":[["The standardized offer specifies the energy-carrying variety, delivery period, supply identifier, and injection location, and submits a single supply quantity q_b and unit valuation v_b.","Declarations are made period by period within the complete trading window, and not every hour is required to be a supply offer; the example submits before each hourly delivery, other period lengths may be used, and updates may be made between adjacent clearings.","Multiple offers with different quantities and prices can construct a step supply curve without offer dependencies; indivisible offers and conditions set within the same clearing based on another hour's clearing result are prohibited."]],"members":[{"id":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R002::V::bidding.supply","rule_id":"v141-c-R002","market_meaning":"Each supply bid specifies an energy carrier, delivery-hour, supply status and network injection location, and states one quantity and one valuation. Scope: Supply bids in the proposed local multi-energy-carrier auction. Supply bids follow the full trading-horizon submission schedule, with separate bids for separate delivery periods; this does not prescribe that every hour's bid must be a supply bid. Scope: Supply bids within agents' rolling trading-horizon submissions. Agents are allowed to update their supply bids between market clearings. Scope: Updates to supply bids in rolling-horizon operation. Condition: Between successive market clearings. Supply bids are submitted once per hour, shortly before the beginning of each delivery-hour. Scope: Supply-bid submission timing under the paper's assumed hourly trading periods. Condition: The described schedule assumes 1 h time-periods; the design permits longer or shorter periods. Agents may submit multiple supply bids with different quantities and valuations to construct a step-function curve without using bid dependencies. Scope: Permitted construction of supply bid curves. Condition: When constructing a step-function bid curve. Agents cannot submit indivisible supply bids that must be either fully accepted or rejected entirely. Scope: Supply-bid admissibility in the proposed market design. Supply bids in one hour cannot be conditioned on the outcomes of another hour within the same market clearing. Scope: Supply bids for different hours within one market clearing. Condition: Conditioning a bid in one hour on another hour's outcome within the same clearing.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"bidding","context_text":"Permitted construction of supply bid curves. | Supply bids for different hours within one market clearing. | Supply bids in the proposed local multi-energy-carrier auction. | Supply bids within agents' rolling trading-horizon submissions. | Supply-bid admissibility in the proposed market design. | Supply-bid submission timing under the paper's assumed hourly trading periods. | Updates to supply bids in rolling-horizon operation.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E012","v141-b-g01-E013","v141-b-g01-E014","v141-b-g01-E015","v141-b-g01-E020","v141-b-g02-E22","v141-b-g02-E25"]},"constraint_refs":["48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R002::v141-c-R002-C001","48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R002::v141-c-R002-C002","48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R002::v141-c-R002-C003","48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R002::v141-c-R002-C004","48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R002::v141-c-R002-C005","48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R002::v141-c-R002-C006","48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R002::v141-c-R002-C007"],"decision_anchor":"bidding.supply","source_rule_sha256":"59314ae7d698a536104e3d9275e52ad2d6a1deaa54f45d082eb628eac452b628","paper":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market","rule_ref":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R002","node_id":"bidding.supply","function":"bidding.supply","unit_id":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-a-M01::bidding.supply","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","anchor":true},{"id":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R003::V::bidding.supply","rule_id":"v141-c-R003","market_meaning":"Submitted demand bids provide inputs to local market clearing. Scope: Supply-and-demand inputs to the local multi-energy-carrier auction. The requested quantity submitted in a demand bid limits the quantity cleared from that bid: clearing cannot exceed its bid quantity. Scope: The cleared quantity of each demand bid in the local auction. Submitted supply bids provide inputs to local market clearing. Scope: Supply-and-demand inputs to the local multi-energy-carrier auction. The offered quantity submitted in a supply bid limits the quantity cleared from that bid: clearing cannot exceed its bid quantity. Scope: The cleared quantity of each supply bid in the local auction. The solution of the consumer-and-producer-surplus optimization determines which bids are accepted or rejected in local clearing. Scope: Allocation decisions produced by the local market's surplus-maximizing optimization. The local market operator operates the clearing function. Scope: Operation of the local market clearing function. Receipt of demand submissions forms part of the joint all-bids-received condition under which the operator clears the local market. Scope: The centralized two-sided auction's joint all-bids receipt condition. Condition: All bids for the auction have been received, encompassing both supply and demand submissions. Receipt of supply submissions forms part of the joint all-bids-received condition under which the operator clears the local market. Scope: The centralized two-sided auction's joint all-bids receipt condition. Condition: All bids for the auction have been received, encompassing both supply and demand submissions. The design clears multiple energy carriers simultaneously through one common optimization. Scope: Common local clearing of multiple energy carriers. The market is cleared once per hour, shortly before each delivery-hour begins. Scope: The paper's rolling-horizon implementation with one-hour delivery periods. Condition: The time-period length is assumed to be 1 h. Each clearing returns results for the full trading horizon. Results for the upcoming binding hour are final, while results for subsequent advisory hours are updated in later clearings. Scope: Allocation results across the rolling trading horizon. Centralized local clearing decides how to dispatch these assets optimally. Scope: Assets whose flexibility is represented using the model's bid-dependency instruments. Condition: Agents apply bid dependencies to provide asset flexibility to the market. Partial clearing of bids is permitted. Scope: Acceptance of bids in the proposed local market. The amount cleared from a bid must be nonnegative. Scope: The cleared amount of every bid. Net energy injection must equal net outflow at each pricing location, ensuring that total supply equals total demand for each time-period and energy carrier. Scope: Each pricing location, time-period and energy carrier in local clearing. Clearing must respect network transfer limitations so that accepted bid combinations do not produce flows beyond local distribution-network capabilities; transfers between adjacent pricing locations are bounded by transfer capacity. Scope: Network-constrained allocations between carrier-specific pricing locations within the local market. The same proportion of every bid in the dependency must clear. Scope: Local clearing of bids in the same AND-dependency. Condition: Bids are included in an AND-dependency. The total accepted quantity from the dependency's bids must not exceed the specified amount. Scope: Local clearing of bids in an LE-dependency. Condition: The dependency type is LE. The total accepted quantity from the dependency's bids must be at least the specified amount. Scope: Local clearing of bids in a GE-dependency. Condition: The dependency type is GE. The total accepted quantity from the dependency's bids must equal the specified amount. Scope: Local clearing of bids in an EQ-dependency. Condition: The dependency type is EQ. The sum of the cleared fractions of the dependency's bids must not exceed one. Scope: Local clearing of bids in the same OR-dependency, including partial acceptance. Condition: Bids are included in an OR-dependency. An individual out-of-the-money bid may be accepted only with compensating bids that make its dependency collectively in-the-money. Scope: Acceptance of individual bids connected by AND-dependencies or OR-dependencies. Condition: An individual bid is out-of-the-money and other bids in its dependency compensate for it so that the dependency altogether is in-the-money. No bids in the OR-dependency clear when the dependency as a whole is unprofitable. Scope: The implemented inequality formulation of an OR-dependency. Condition: The bid dependency as a whole is unprofitable. The proportion of district heat supplied from low-temperature sources must be restricted to ensure that the water reaches a sufficiently high temperature. Scope: District-heating allocations involving low-temperature heat sources. Condition: Heat sources deliver below the target temperature of the district-heating system.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"clearing","context_text":"Acceptance of bids in the proposed local market. | Acceptance of individual bids connected by AND-dependencies or OR-dependencies. | Allocation decisions produced by the local market's surplus-maximizing optimization. | Allocation results across the rolling trading horizon. | Assets whose flexibility is represented using the model's bid-dependency instruments. | Common local clearing of multiple energy carriers. | District-heating allocations involving low-temperature heat sources. | Each pricing location, time-period and energy carrier in local clearing. | Local clearing of bids in a GE-dependency. | Local clearing of bids in an EQ-dependency. | Local clearing of bids in an LE-dependency. | Local clearing of bids in the same AND-dependency. | Local clearing of bids in the same OR-dependency, including partial acceptance. | Network-constrained allocations between carrier-specific pricing locations within the local market. | Operation of the local market clearing function. | Supply-and-demand inputs to the local multi-energy-carrier auction. | The centralized two-sided auction's joint all-bids receipt condition. | The cleared amount of every bid. | The cleared quantity of each demand bid in the local auction. | The cleared quantity of each supply bid in the local auction. | The implemented inequality formulation of an OR-dependency. | The paper's rolling-horizon implementation with one-hour delivery periods.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E001","v141-b-g01-E006","v141-b-g01-E007","v141-b-g01-E012","v141-b-g01-E013","v141-b-g01-E018","v141-b-g01-E019","v141-b-g01-E021","v141-b-g01-E022","v141-b-g01-E023","v141-b-g01-E024","v141-b-g01-E025","v141-b-g01-E029","v141-b-g01-E030","v141-b-g01-E035","v141-b-g01-E036","v141-b-g01-E037","v141-b-g01-E040","v141-b-g01-E043","v141-b-g02-E24","v141-b-g03-E01"]},"constraint_refs":["48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C003","48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C004","48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C008"],"decision_anchor":"clearing.local","source_rule_sha256":"b076e845b970ccb25427033e8aeaf1f2e24082638406e79e7630909ce0326898","paper":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market","rule_ref":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R003","node_id":"bidding.supply","function":"bidding.supply","unit_id":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-a-M01::bidding.supply","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","anchor":false},{"id":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R004::V::bidding.supply","rule_id":"v141-c-R004","market_meaning":"Demand submissions provide bid inputs to the welfare-maximizing market-clearing optimization. Scope: Market-clearing optimization of the proposed local multi-energy-carrier auction. Supply submissions provide bid inputs to the welfare-maximizing market-clearing optimization. Scope: Market-clearing optimization of the proposed local multi-energy-carrier auction. The clearing objective maximizes consumer and producer surplus, defined as the total valuation of cleared demand bids minus the total valuation of cleared supply bids. Scope: Market-clearing optimization of the proposed local multi-energy-carrier auction.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"clearing","context_text":"Market-clearing optimization of the proposed local multi-energy-carrier auction.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E022","v141-b-g01-E023"]},"constraint_refs":["48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R004::v141-c-R004-C002"],"decision_anchor":"clearing.social_welfare","source_rule_sha256":"08c2f7c4f7d8b4941f3f1dcf8f413dc0143755df5d507d9a78a6dae93b15d539","paper":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market","rule_ref":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R004","node_id":"bidding.supply","function":"bidding.supply","unit_id":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-a-M01::bidding.supply","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","anchor":false},{"id":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R005::V::bidding.supply","rule_id":"v141-c-R005","market_meaning":"Demand bids are submitted to the central market operator at a specific time and in accordance with a standardized bid format. Scope: Scheduled bid submission in the centralized two-sided local auction. Supply bids are submitted to the central market operator at a specific time and in accordance with a standardized bid format. Scope: Scheduled bid submission in the centralized two-sided local auction. The market operator is responsible for continuous operation of the local market and its supporting functions. Scope: Continuous operation of the local market and its supporting functions. The market operator should preferably be financially independent from the owners of market participants. Scope: Financial relationship between the market operator and market-participant owners. The market operator informs each agent whether or not its bids cleared. Scope: Communication of bid-clearing outcomes to agents in the local auction.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"Communication of bid-clearing outcomes to agents in the local auction. | Continuous operation of the local market and its supporting functions. | Financial relationship between the market operator and market-participant owners. | Scheduled bid submission in the centralized two-sided local auction.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E006","v141-b-g01-E007","v141-b-g01-E015"]},"constraint_refs":["48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C002"],"decision_anchor":"coordination.local_operator","source_rule_sha256":"dcb3931aa1fc833472b99ab46ce93226b54019b660f5a22ab36f0ad4b43cfe12","paper":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market","rule_ref":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R005","node_id":"bidding.supply","function":"bidding.supply","unit_id":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-a-M01::bidding.supply","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","anchor":false},{"id":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R007::V::bidding.supply","rule_id":"v141-c-R007","market_meaning":"The local clearing price equals the valuation contained in the highest-valued rejected demand bid when that bid is marginal. Scope: Marginal-bid price determination in the local auction. Condition: There are no network constraints or bid dependencies, and the highest-valued rejected demand bid is marginal. The local clearing price equals the valuation contained in the highest-valued accepted supply bid when that bid is marginal. Scope: Marginal-bid price determination in the local auction. Condition: There are no network constraints or bid dependencies, and the highest-valued accepted supply bid is marginal. Local market clearing outputs market prices that must be compatible with its cleared-bid solution. Scope: Outputs of the proposed local multi-energy-carrier market clearing. The local market operator determines one uniform clearing price for each time-period, energy carrier and pricing location. Scope: Uniform pricing within each time-period, energy carrier and pricing location of the local market. Local clearing prices need not be equal across energy carriers, even when the carriers are cleared simultaneously. Scope: Prices for energy carriers cleared simultaneously in the local market. Prices at the local market's pricing locations adjust to reflect the marginal value of energy at each location. Scope: Energy-carrier-specific pricing locations within the local market. Condition: Network congestion occurs. Local clearing prices can be obtained from the shadow prices of the power-balance constraints. Scope: Recovery of local clearing prices from the proposed optimization formulation. Condition: The optimization problem is linear and its variables take values on a closed interval of real numbers. Shadow prices continue to provide appropriate local market clearing prices when bids have AND- or OR-dependencies. Scope: Shadow-price recovery of prices in the local market with linked bids. Condition: Bids are connected with AND-dependencies or OR-dependencies. The shadow prices of the power-balance constraints differ across pricing locations. Scope: Prices across pricing locations within the local market. Condition: Network limitations are implemented.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"pricing","context_text":"Energy-carrier-specific pricing locations within the local market. | Marginal-bid price determination in the local auction. | Outputs of the proposed local multi-energy-carrier market clearing. | Prices across pricing locations within the local market. | Prices for energy carriers cleared simultaneously in the local market. | Recovery of local clearing prices from the proposed optimization formulation. | Shadow-price recovery of prices in the local market with linked bids. | Uniform pricing within each time-period, energy carrier and pricing location of the local market.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E009","v141-b-g01-E010","v141-b-g01-E015","v141-b-g01-E021","v141-b-g01-E022","v141-b-g01-E040","v141-b-g01-E041","v141-b-g01-E042","v141-b-g01-E043"]},"constraint_refs":["48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R007::v141-c-R007-C002"],"decision_anchor":"pricing.local","source_rule_sha256":"cebe08bdbd281691f3dc4d810d593fac07465ea6e3f0aea76ccec7c989aa2a8e","paper":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market","rule_ref":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R007","node_id":"bidding.supply","function":"bidding.supply","unit_id":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-a-M01::bidding.supply","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","anchor":false}],"paper_ids":["48-multiple_energy_carrier_market"],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E015","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p04-c1r2__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"energy will be injected or withdrawn). In addition, each bid states a 4. single quantity (in kWh) an","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"In the proposed market design, each individual bid has a very simple structure. Each bid contains basic information about what the bid is for (i.e. it specifies an energy carrier, a delivery-hour, whether it is a supply or demand bid, and the location on the network where the energy will be injected or withdrawn). In addition, each bid states a single quantity (in kWh) and a single valuation (in €/kWh).","paper":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market","rule_id":"v141-c-R002","quote":"In the proposed market design, each individual bid has a very simple structure. Each bid contains basic information about what the bid is for (i.e. it specifies an energy carrier, a delivery-hour, whether it is a supply or demand bid, and the location on the network where the energy will be injected or withdrawn). In addition, each bid states a single quantity (in kWh) and a single valuation (in €/kWh)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E012","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p03-c2r3__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"4.1.3. Rolling time-horizon a- Energy is traded for discrete time-periods, and the time-periodn- len","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Energy is traded for discrete time-periods, and the time-period length is the same for all energy carriers. Energy in different time-periods are traded as different commodities, and agents submit separate bids for separate time-periods. For clarity, we will here assume that the time-period length is 1 h. However, the time-period length could be both longer and shorter.","paper":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market","rule_id":"v141-c-R002","quote":"Energy is traded for discrete time-periods, and the time-period length is the same for all energy carriers. Energy in different time-periods are traded as different commodities, and agents submit separate bids for separate time-periods. For clarity, we will here assume that the time-period length is 1 h. However, the time-period length could be both longer and shorter."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E014","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p04-c1r1__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"M. Brolin and H. Pihl agents submit bids for all hours in the trading horizon, and they are 4. allow","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"agents submit bids for all hours in the trading horizon, and they are allowed to update their bids between market clearings.","paper":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market","rule_id":"v141-c-R002","quote":"agents submit bids for all hours in the trading horizon, and they are allowed to update their bids between market clearings."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E013","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p03-c2r3__v141-a-M01-settlement","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"4.1.3. Rolling time-horizon a- Energy is traded for discrete time-periods, and the time-periodn- len","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"In order to minimize forecast errors, bid submission and market clearing take place as close to the delivery-hour as possible. Therefore, bids are submitted and the market is cleared once per hour, shortly before the beginning of each delivery-hour. However, for the market to be able to accommodate dependencies over longer periods of time, each market clearing also includes a range of future hours. The full range of hours included in a market clearing is referred to as the trading horizon. The first hour in the trading horizon (the upcoming delivery-hour) is referred to as the binding hour, and subsequent hours are referred to as advisory hours. As the names indicate, the market results for the binding hour are final, whereas the results for the advisory hours will be updated in subsequent market clearings.","paper":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market","rule_id":"v141-c-R002","quote":"In order to minimize forecast errors, bid submission and market clearing take place as close to the delivery-hour as possible. Therefore, bids are submitted and the market is cleared once per hour, shortly before the beginning of each delivery-hour. However, for the market to be able to accommodate dependencies over longer periods of time, each market clearing also includes a range of future hours. The full range of hours included in a market clearing is referred to as the trading horizon. The first hour in the trading horizon (the upcoming delivery-hour) is referred to as the binding hour, and subsequent hours are referred to as advisory hours. As the names indicate, the market results for the binding hour are final, whereas the results for the advisory hours will be updated in subsequent market clearings."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E020","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p04-c1r3__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"GE-dependencies: The sum of the accepted quantity from the bids qb • should be greater than or equal","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"Note that agents can construct some bid combinations without the need to use bid dependencies. For example, step-function bid curves can be built by simply submitting multiple bids with different quantities and valuations.","paper":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market","rule_id":"v141-c-R002","quote":"Note that agents can construct some bid combinations without the need to use bid dependencies. For example, step-function bid curves can be built by simply submitting multiple bids with different quantities and valuations."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E22","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p08-c1r4__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":"6.1. The indivisibility issue","anchor_text":"producer may have a minimum load requirement such that it has to either be turned oﬀor operate above","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"exception"},"source_text":"As described in 4.2, the market optimization problem is linear and no integer variables are introduced. This means that there is no possibility for agents to submit indivisible bids, i.e. bids that should be either fully accepted or not accepted at all.","paper":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market","rule_id":"v141-c-R002","quote":"As described in 4.2, the market optimization problem is linear and no integer variables are introduced. This means that there is no possibility for agents to submit indivisible bids, i.e. bids that should be either fully accepted or not accepted at all."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E25","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p08-c2r4__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":"6.3. Multiple energy carriers and flexibility instruments","anchor_text":"to Even though the proposed ﬂexibility instruments provide a vast list le of options and possibiliti","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"exception"},"source_text":"Even though the proposed flexibility instruments provide a vast list of options and possibilities, there are limitations in what they can represent. For example, since agents cannot submit indivisible bids, the possibility for a market participant to completely switch between electricity and DH cannot be ensured, i.e. it cannot be ensured that only one of these options exclusively will be cleared. Another limitation is the difficulty to construct bids for energy storage that takes full advantage of the flexibility offered by such assets. Although it is possible to construct bids and bid dependencies that represent a specific charge and discharge cycle, it is difficult to fully capture all possibilities and constraints of a typical energy storage. Accurately capturing all possible charge and discharge possibilities over a trading horizon would require a very large number of bids and bid dependencies. Further, the available capacity for hours further out in the horizon depends on the amount cleared in prior hours. However, it is not possible to condition the bids in one hour on the outcomes of another hour within the same market clearing.","paper":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market","rule_id":"v141-c-R002","quote":"Even though the proposed flexibility instruments provide a vast list of options and possibilities, there are limitations in what they can represent. For example, since agents cannot submit indivisible bids, the possibility for a market participant to completely switch between electricity and DH cannot be ensured, i.e. it cannot be ensured that only one of these options exclusively will be cleared. Another limitation is the difficulty to construct bids for energy storage that takes full advantage of the flexibility offered by such assets. Although it is possible to construct bids and bid dependencies that represent a specific charge and discharge cycle, it is difficult to fully capture all possibilities and constraints of a typical energy storage. Accurately capturing all possible charge and discharge possibilities over a trading horizon would require a very large number of bids and bid dependencies. Further, the available capacity for hours further out in the horizon depends on the amount cleared in prior hours. However, it is not possible to condition the bids in one hour on the outcomes of another hour within the same market clearing."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E006","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p03-c1r4__v141-a-M01-participation","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"the local market and other surrounding energy systems. A retailer uptherefore does not represent a p","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The local market clearing function is matching the submitted supply and demand bids, taking into account aspects such as grid constraints. The clearing function is operated by a market operator, which is responsible for the continuous operation of the local market and its supporting functions, and should therefore preferably be financially independent from the owners of the market participants.","paper":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market","rule_id":"v141-c-R003","quote":"The local market clearing function is matching the submitted supply and demand bids, taking into account aspects such as grid constraints. The clearing function is operated by a market operator, which is responsible for the continuous operation of the local market and its supporting functions, and should therefore preferably be financially independent from the owners of the market participants."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E022","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p04-c2r1__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Electrical Power and Energy Systems 118 (2020) 105739 re 4.2. Market clearing and pricing re This se","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"This section provides a mathematical description of the market clearing mechanism, including all the main ingredients discussed in Section 4.1. The market clearing is based on mathematical optimization, where the objective is to maximize the sum of consumer and producer surplus. The problem is kept linear, which means that it can be solved efficiently using available linear programming (LP) software. Input to the market clearing problem consists of bids and bid dependencies, and outputs are the cleared bid quantities and market prices.","paper":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market","rule_id":"v141-c-R003","quote":"This section provides a mathematical description of the market clearing mechanism, including all the main ingredients discussed in Section 4.1. The market clearing is based on mathematical optimization, where the objective is to maximize the sum of consumer and producer surplus. The problem is kept linear, which means that it can be solved efficiently using available linear programming (LP) software. Input to the market clearing problem consists of bids and bid dependencies, and outputs are the cleared bid quantities and market prices."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E001","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p02-c1r1__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":2,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"M. Brolin and H. Pihl Nomenclature L0 Ll Algebraic symbols vb qb B , b set and index of bids Q D , d","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"B, b set and index of bids; D, d set and index of demand bids, D ⊂ B; S, s set and index of supply bids, S ⊂ B; R, r set and index of bid dependencies; R^X set of bid dependencies of type X, R^X ⊂ R; T, t set and index of time steps; E, e set and index of energy carriers; L, l set and index of pricing locations.","paper":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market","rule_id":"v141-c-R003","quote":"B, b set and index of bids; D, d set and index of demand bids, D ⊂ B; S, s set and index of supply bids, S ⊂ B; R, r set and index of bid dependencies; R^X set of bid dependencies of type X, R^X ⊂ R; T, t set and index of time steps; E, e set and index of energy carriers; L, l set and index of pricing locations."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E024","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p04-c2r2__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"a 4.2.1. Objective and bid dependencies m The objective for the optimization problem is to maximize ","equation_id":"(2)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The amount to clear from each bid should be non-negative and cannot exceed the bid quantity: 0 \\leqslant y_b \\leqslant q_b, \\quad \\forall b \\in B. \\tag{2}","paper":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market","rule_id":"v141-c-R003","quote":"The amount to clear from each bid should be non-negative and cannot exceed the bid quantity: 0 \\leqslant y_b \\leqslant q_b, \\quad \\forall b \\in B. \\tag{2}"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E007","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p03-c2r1__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Electrical Power and Energy Systems 118 (2020) 105739 of 4.1. Main ingredients s- se 4.1.1. Centrali","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Like many wholesale electricity markets, the proposed market is based on a centralized two-sided auction format. It is a centralized auction in the sense that all agents submit bids to a central market operator, at a specific time and in accordance with a standardized bid format. Once all bids have been received, the market operator clears the market, meaning that it identifies which bids should be accepted, based on the information contained in the bids. The market operator informs each agent whether or not their bids cleared.","paper":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market","rule_id":"v141-c-R003","quote":"Like many wholesale electricity markets, the proposed market is based on a centralized two-sided auction format. It is a centralized auction in the sense that all agents submit bids to a central market operator, at a specific time and in accordance with a standardized bid format. Once all bids have been received, the market operator clears the market, meaning that it identifies which bids should be accepted, based on the information contained in the bids. The market operator informs each agent whether or not their bids cleared."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E022","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p04-c2r1__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Electrical Power and Energy Systems 118 (2020) 105739 re 4.2. Market clearing and pricing re This se","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"This section provides a mathematical description of the market clearing mechanism, including all the main ingredients discussed in Section 4.1. The market clearing is based on mathematical optimization, where the objective is to maximize the sum of consumer and producer surplus. The problem is kept linear, which means that it can be solved efficiently using available linear programming (LP) software. Input to the market clearing problem consists of bids and bid dependencies, and outputs are the cleared bid quantities and market prices.","paper":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market","rule_id":"v141-c-R004","quote":"This section provides a mathematical description of the market clearing mechanism, including all the main ingredients discussed in Section 4.1. The market clearing is based on mathematical optimization, where the objective is to maximize the sum of consumer and producer surplus. The problem is kept linear, which means that it can be solved efficiently using available linear programming (LP) software. Input to the market clearing problem consists of bids and bid dependencies, and outputs are the cleared bid quantities and market prices."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E023","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p04-c2r2__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"a 4.2.1. Objective and bid dependencies m The objective for the optimization problem is to maximize ","equation_id":"(1)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The objective for the optimization problem is to maximize consumer and producer surplus, i.e. the difference between the sum of the valuations of all cleared demand bids and the sum of the valuations of all cleared supply bids. The optimization variables are y_b, denoting the amount to clear from each bid. \\max_{y_b} \\left[ \\sum_{b \\in D} v_b \\cdot y_b - \\sum_{b \\in S} v_b \\cdot y_b \\right] \\tag{1}","paper":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market","rule_id":"v141-c-R004","quote":"The objective for the optimization problem is to maximize consumer and producer surplus, i.e. the difference between the sum of the valuations of all cleared demand bids and the sum of the valuations of all cleared supply bids. The optimization variables are y_b, denoting the amount to clear from each bid. \\max_{y_b} \\left[ \\sum_{b \\in D} v_b \\cdot y_b - \\sum_{b \\in S} v_b \\cdot y_b \\right] \\tag{1}"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E007","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p03-c2r1__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Electrical Power and Energy Systems 118 (2020) 105739 of 4.1. Main ingredients s- se 4.1.1. Centrali","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Like many wholesale electricity markets, the proposed market is based on a centralized two-sided auction format. It is a centralized auction in the sense that all agents submit bids to a central market operator, at a specific time and in accordance with a standardized bid format. Once all bids have been received, the market operator clears the market, meaning that it identifies which bids should be accepted, based on the information contained in the bids. The market operator informs each agent whether or not their bids cleared.","paper":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market","rule_id":"v141-c-R005","quote":"Like many wholesale electricity markets, the proposed market is based on a centralized two-sided auction format. It is a centralized auction in the sense that all agents submit bids to a central market operator, at a specific time and in accordance with a standardized bid format. Once all bids have been received, the market operator clears the market, meaning that it identifies which bids should be accepted, based on the information contained in the bids. The market operator informs each agent whether or not their bids cleared."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E015","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p04-c1r2__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"energy will be injected or withdrawn). In addition, each bid states a 4. single quantity (in kWh) an","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"In the proposed market design, each individual bid has a very simple structure. Each bid contains basic information about what the bid is for (i.e. it specifies an energy carrier, a delivery-hour, whether it is a supply or demand bid, and the location on the network where the energy will be injected or withdrawn). In addition, each bid states a single quantity (in kWh) and a single valuation (in €/kWh).","paper":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market","rule_id":"v141-c-R005","quote":"In the proposed market design, each individual bid has a very simple structure. Each bid contains basic information about what the bid is for (i.e. it specifies an energy carrier, a delivery-hour, whether it is a supply or demand bid, and the location on the network where the energy will be injected or withdrawn). In addition, each bid states a single quantity (in kWh) and a single valuation (in €/kWh)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E015","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p04-c1r2__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"energy will be injected or withdrawn). In addition, each bid states a 4. single quantity (in kWh) an","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"In the proposed market design, each individual bid has a very simple structure. Each bid contains basic information about what the bid is for (i.e. it specifies an energy carrier, a delivery-hour, whether it is a supply or demand bid, and the location on the network where the energy will be injected or withdrawn). In addition, each bid states a single quantity (in kWh) and a single valuation (in €/kWh).","paper":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market","rule_id":"v141-c-R007","quote":"In the proposed market design, each individual bid has a very simple structure. Each bid contains basic information about what the bid is for (i.e. it specifies an energy carrier, a delivery-hour, whether it is a supply or demand bid, and the location on the network where the energy will be injected or withdrawn). In addition, each bid states a single quantity (in kWh) and a single valuation (in €/kWh)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E042","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p05-c2r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"al ( y y), j o- have preferred to trade (they are out-of-the-money). The market clearing prices can ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"In a simple case where there are no network constraints and no bid dependencies, the shadow price for a power balance constraint equals the valuation of the highest-valued accepted supply bid, or the highest-valued rejected demand bid, depending on which is marginal. Therefore, the shadow prices are market clearing in this simple case.","paper":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market","rule_id":"v141-c-R007","quote":"In a simple case where there are no network constraints and no bid dependencies, the shadow price for a power balance constraint equals the valuation of the highest-valued accepted supply bid, or the highest-valued rejected demand bid, depending on which is marginal. Therefore, the shadow prices are market clearing in this simple case."}],"candidate_only":true,"classification_subtypes":["supply_quantity_valuation_submission"],"projection_statuses":["clear"],"taxonomy":{"primary_family":"KG40-L3-SC-L3-bb9e7457976d4f9a","secondary_families":[],"stage":"L3","ontological_kind":"SC-L3-bb9e7457976d4f9a"},"semantic_definition":{"definition":"The supplier submits the supply quantity and unit valuation according to the energy-carrying commodity identifier, forming an energy-commodity auction input not limited to electricity.","identity_fields":["Submitter: energy-commodity supplier","Object: supply quantity and valuation identified by energy-carrying variety","Function: provide supply-side clearing input for the commodity"]},"source_units":[{"unit_id":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-a-M01::bidding.supply","paper_id":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","function":"bidding.supply","source_occurrences":[{"id":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R002::V::bidding.supply","rule_id":"v141-c-R002","market_meaning":"Each supply bid specifies an energy carrier, delivery-hour, supply status and network injection location, and states one quantity and one valuation. Scope: Supply bids in the proposed local multi-energy-carrier auction. Supply bids follow the full trading-horizon submission schedule, with separate bids for separate delivery periods; this does not prescribe that every hour's bid must be a supply bid. Scope: Supply bids within agents' rolling trading-horizon submissions. Agents are allowed to update their supply bids between market clearings. Scope: Updates to supply bids in rolling-horizon operation. Condition: Between successive market clearings. Supply bids are submitted once per hour, shortly before the beginning of each delivery-hour. Scope: Supply-bid submission timing under the paper's assumed hourly trading periods. Condition: The described schedule assumes 1 h time-periods; the design permits longer or shorter periods. Agents may submit multiple supply bids with different quantities and valuations to construct a step-function curve without using bid dependencies. Scope: Permitted construction of supply bid curves. Condition: When constructing a step-function bid curve. Agents cannot submit indivisible supply bids that must be either fully accepted or rejected entirely. Scope: Supply-bid admissibility in the proposed market design. Supply bids in one hour cannot be conditioned on the outcomes of another hour within the same market clearing. Scope: Supply bids for different hours within one market clearing. Condition: Conditioning a bid in one hour on another hour's outcome within the same clearing.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"bidding","context_text":"Permitted construction of supply bid curves. | Supply bids for different hours within one market clearing. | Supply bids in the proposed local multi-energy-carrier auction. | Supply bids within agents' rolling trading-horizon submissions. | Supply-bid admissibility in the proposed market design. | Supply-bid submission timing under the paper's assumed hourly trading periods. | Updates to supply bids in rolling-horizon operation.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E012","v141-b-g01-E013","v141-b-g01-E014","v141-b-g01-E015","v141-b-g01-E020","v141-b-g02-E22","v141-b-g02-E25"]},"constraint_refs":["48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R002::v141-c-R002-C001","48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R002::v141-c-R002-C002","48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R002::v141-c-R002-C003","48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R002::v141-c-R002-C004","48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R002::v141-c-R002-C005","48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R002::v141-c-R002-C006","48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R002::v141-c-R002-C007"],"decision_anchor":"bidding.supply","source_rule_sha256":"59314ae7d698a536104e3d9275e52ad2d6a1deaa54f45d082eb628eac452b628"},{"id":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R003::V::bidding.supply","rule_id":"v141-c-R003","market_meaning":"Submitted demand bids provide inputs to local market clearing. Scope: Supply-and-demand inputs to the local multi-energy-carrier auction. The requested quantity submitted in a demand bid limits the quantity cleared from that bid: clearing cannot exceed its bid quantity. Scope: The cleared quantity of each demand bid in the local auction. Submitted supply bids provide inputs to local market clearing. Scope: Supply-and-demand inputs to the local multi-energy-carrier auction. The offered quantity submitted in a supply bid limits the quantity cleared from that bid: clearing cannot exceed its bid quantity. Scope: The cleared quantity of each supply bid in the local auction. The solution of the consumer-and-producer-surplus optimization determines which bids are accepted or rejected in local clearing. Scope: Allocation decisions produced by the local market's surplus-maximizing optimization. The local market operator operates the clearing function. Scope: Operation of the local market clearing function. Receipt of demand submissions forms part of the joint all-bids-received condition under which the operator clears the local market. Scope: The centralized two-sided auction's joint all-bids receipt condition. Condition: All bids for the auction have been received, encompassing both supply and demand submissions. Receipt of supply submissions forms part of the joint all-bids-received condition under which the operator clears the local market. Scope: The centralized two-sided auction's joint all-bids receipt condition. Condition: All bids for the auction have been received, encompassing both supply and demand submissions. The design clears multiple energy carriers simultaneously through one common optimization. Scope: Common local clearing of multiple energy carriers. The market is cleared once per hour, shortly before each delivery-hour begins. Scope: The paper's rolling-horizon implementation with one-hour delivery periods. Condition: The time-period length is assumed to be 1 h. Each clearing returns results for the full trading horizon. Results for the upcoming binding hour are final, while results for subsequent advisory hours are updated in later clearings. Scope: Allocation results across the rolling trading horizon. Centralized local clearing decides how to dispatch these assets optimally. Scope: Assets whose flexibility is represented using the model's bid-dependency instruments. Condition: Agents apply bid dependencies to provide asset flexibility to the market. Partial clearing of bids is permitted. Scope: Acceptance of bids in the proposed local market. The amount cleared from a bid must be nonnegative. Scope: The cleared amount of every bid. Net energy injection must equal net outflow at each pricing location, ensuring that total supply equals total demand for each time-period and energy carrier. Scope: Each pricing location, time-period and energy carrier in local clearing. Clearing must respect network transfer limitations so that accepted bid combinations do not produce flows beyond local distribution-network capabilities; transfers between adjacent pricing locations are bounded by transfer capacity. Scope: Network-constrained allocations between carrier-specific pricing locations within the local market. The same proportion of every bid in the dependency must clear. Scope: Local clearing of bids in the same AND-dependency. Condition: Bids are included in an AND-dependency. The total accepted quantity from the dependency's bids must not exceed the specified amount. Scope: Local clearing of bids in an LE-dependency. Condition: The dependency type is LE. The total accepted quantity from the dependency's bids must be at least the specified amount. Scope: Local clearing of bids in a GE-dependency. Condition: The dependency type is GE. The total accepted quantity from the dependency's bids must equal the specified amount. Scope: Local clearing of bids in an EQ-dependency. Condition: The dependency type is EQ. The sum of the cleared fractions of the dependency's bids must not exceed one. Scope: Local clearing of bids in the same OR-dependency, including partial acceptance. Condition: Bids are included in an OR-dependency. An individual out-of-the-money bid may be accepted only with compensating bids that make its dependency collectively in-the-money. Scope: Acceptance of individual bids connected by AND-dependencies or OR-dependencies. Condition: An individual bid is out-of-the-money and other bids in its dependency compensate for it so that the dependency altogether is in-the-money. No bids in the OR-dependency clear when the dependency as a whole is unprofitable. Scope: The implemented inequality formulation of an OR-dependency. Condition: The bid dependency as a whole is unprofitable. The proportion of district heat supplied from low-temperature sources must be restricted to ensure that the water reaches a sufficiently high temperature. Scope: District-heating allocations involving low-temperature heat sources. Condition: Heat sources deliver below the target temperature of the district-heating system.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"clearing","context_text":"Acceptance of bids in the proposed local market. | Acceptance of individual bids connected by AND-dependencies or OR-dependencies. | Allocation decisions produced by the local market's surplus-maximizing optimization. | Allocation results across the rolling trading horizon. | Assets whose flexibility is represented using the model's bid-dependency instruments. | Common local clearing of multiple energy carriers. | District-heating allocations involving low-temperature heat sources. | Each pricing location, time-period and energy carrier in local clearing. | Local clearing of bids in a GE-dependency. | Local clearing of bids in an EQ-dependency. | Local clearing of bids in an LE-dependency. | Local clearing of bids in the same AND-dependency. | Local clearing of bids in the same OR-dependency, including partial acceptance. | Network-constrained allocations between carrier-specific pricing locations within the local market. | Operation of the local market clearing function. | Supply-and-demand inputs to the local multi-energy-carrier auction. | The centralized two-sided auction's joint all-bids receipt condition. | The cleared amount of every bid. | The cleared quantity of each demand bid in the local auction. | The cleared quantity of each supply bid in the local auction. | The implemented inequality formulation of an OR-dependency. | The paper's rolling-horizon implementation with one-hour delivery periods.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E001","v141-b-g01-E006","v141-b-g01-E007","v141-b-g01-E012","v141-b-g01-E013","v141-b-g01-E018","v141-b-g01-E019","v141-b-g01-E021","v141-b-g01-E022","v141-b-g01-E023","v141-b-g01-E024","v141-b-g01-E025","v141-b-g01-E029","v141-b-g01-E030","v141-b-g01-E035","v141-b-g01-E036","v141-b-g01-E037","v141-b-g01-E040","v141-b-g01-E043","v141-b-g02-E24","v141-b-g03-E01"]},"constraint_refs":["48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C003","48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C004","48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C008"],"decision_anchor":"clearing.local","source_rule_sha256":"b076e845b970ccb25427033e8aeaf1f2e24082638406e79e7630909ce0326898"},{"id":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R004::V::bidding.supply","rule_id":"v141-c-R004","market_meaning":"Demand submissions provide bid inputs to the welfare-maximizing market-clearing optimization. Scope: Market-clearing optimization of the proposed local multi-energy-carrier auction. Supply submissions provide bid inputs to the welfare-maximizing market-clearing optimization. Scope: Market-clearing optimization of the proposed local multi-energy-carrier auction. The clearing objective maximizes consumer and producer surplus, defined as the total valuation of cleared demand bids minus the total valuation of cleared supply bids. Scope: Market-clearing optimization of the proposed local multi-energy-carrier auction.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"clearing","context_text":"Market-clearing optimization of the proposed local multi-energy-carrier auction.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E022","v141-b-g01-E023"]},"constraint_refs":["48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R004::v141-c-R004-C002"],"decision_anchor":"clearing.social_welfare","source_rule_sha256":"08c2f7c4f7d8b4941f3f1dcf8f413dc0143755df5d507d9a78a6dae93b15d539"},{"id":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R005::V::bidding.supply","rule_id":"v141-c-R005","market_meaning":"Demand bids are submitted to the central market operator at a specific time and in accordance with a standardized bid format. Scope: Scheduled bid submission in the centralized two-sided local auction. Supply bids are submitted to the central market operator at a specific time and in accordance with a standardized bid format. Scope: Scheduled bid submission in the centralized two-sided local auction. The market operator is responsible for continuous operation of the local market and its supporting functions. Scope: Continuous operation of the local market and its supporting functions. The market operator should preferably be financially independent from the owners of market participants. Scope: Financial relationship between the market operator and market-participant owners. The market operator informs each agent whether or not its bids cleared. Scope: Communication of bid-clearing outcomes to agents in the local auction.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"Communication of bid-clearing outcomes to agents in the local auction. | Continuous operation of the local market and its supporting functions. | Financial relationship between the market operator and market-participant owners. | Scheduled bid submission in the centralized two-sided local auction.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E006","v141-b-g01-E007","v141-b-g01-E015"]},"constraint_refs":["48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C002"],"decision_anchor":"coordination.local_operator","source_rule_sha256":"dcb3931aa1fc833472b99ab46ce93226b54019b660f5a22ab36f0ad4b43cfe12"},{"id":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R007::V::bidding.supply","rule_id":"v141-c-R007","market_meaning":"The local clearing price equals the valuation contained in the highest-valued rejected demand bid when that bid is marginal. Scope: Marginal-bid price determination in the local auction. Condition: There are no network constraints or bid dependencies, and the highest-valued rejected demand bid is marginal. The local clearing price equals the valuation contained in the highest-valued accepted supply bid when that bid is marginal. Scope: Marginal-bid price determination in the local auction. Condition: There are no network constraints or bid dependencies, and the highest-valued accepted supply bid is marginal. Local market clearing outputs market prices that must be compatible with its cleared-bid solution. Scope: Outputs of the proposed local multi-energy-carrier market clearing. The local market operator determines one uniform clearing price for each time-period, energy carrier and pricing location. Scope: Uniform pricing within each time-period, energy carrier and pricing location of the local market. Local clearing prices need not be equal across energy carriers, even when the carriers are cleared simultaneously. Scope: Prices for energy carriers cleared simultaneously in the local market. Prices at the local market's pricing locations adjust to reflect the marginal value of energy at each location. Scope: Energy-carrier-specific pricing locations within the local market. Condition: Network congestion occurs. Local clearing prices can be obtained from the shadow prices of the power-balance constraints. Scope: Recovery of local clearing prices from the proposed optimization formulation. Condition: The optimization problem is linear and its variables take values on a closed interval of real numbers. Shadow prices continue to provide appropriate local market clearing prices when bids have AND- or OR-dependencies. Scope: Shadow-price recovery of prices in the local market with linked bids. Condition: Bids are connected with AND-dependencies or OR-dependencies. The shadow prices of the power-balance constraints differ across pricing locations. Scope: Prices across pricing locations within the local market. Condition: Network limitations are implemented.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"pricing","context_text":"Energy-carrier-specific pricing locations within the local market. | Marginal-bid price determination in the local auction. | Outputs of the proposed local multi-energy-carrier market clearing. | Prices across pricing locations within the local market. | Prices for energy carriers cleared simultaneously in the local market. | Recovery of local clearing prices from the proposed optimization formulation. | Shadow-price recovery of prices in the local market with linked bids. | Uniform pricing within each time-period, energy carrier and pricing location of the local market.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E009","v141-b-g01-E010","v141-b-g01-E015","v141-b-g01-E021","v141-b-g01-E022","v141-b-g01-E040","v141-b-g01-E041","v141-b-g01-E042","v141-b-g01-E043"]},"constraint_refs":["48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R007::v141-c-R007-C002"],"decision_anchor":"pricing.local","source_rule_sha256":"cebe08bdbd281691f3dc4d810d593fac07465ea6e3f0aea76ccec7c989aa2a8e"}],"constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R002-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Each supply bid specifies an energy carrier, delivery-hour, supply status and network injection location, and states one quantity and one valuation. Scope: Supply bids in the proposed local multi-energy-carrier auction.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.supply"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E015"],"ref":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R002::v141-c-R002-C001","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R002","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E015","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p04-c1r2__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"energy will be injected or withdrawn). In addition, each bid states a 4. single quantity (in kWh) an","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"In the proposed market design, each individual bid has a very simple structure. Each bid contains basic information about what the bid is for (i.e. it specifies an energy carrier, a delivery-hour, whether it is a supply or demand bid, and the location on the network where the energy will be injected or withdrawn). In addition, each bid states a single quantity (in kWh) and a single valuation (in €/kWh)."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R002-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Supply bids follow the full trading-horizon submission schedule, with separate bids for separate delivery periods; this does not prescribe that every hour's bid must be a supply bid. Scope: Supply bids within agents' rolling trading-horizon submissions.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.supply"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E012","v141-b-g01-E014"],"ref":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R002::v141-c-R002-C002","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R002","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E012","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p03-c2r3__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"4.1.3. Rolling time-horizon a- Energy is traded for discrete time-periods, and the time-periodn- len","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Energy is traded for discrete time-periods, and the time-period length is the same for all energy carriers. Energy in different time-periods are traded as different commodities, and agents submit separate bids for separate time-periods. For clarity, we will here assume that the time-period length is 1 h. However, the time-period length could be both longer and shorter."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E014","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p04-c1r1__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"M. Brolin and H. Pihl agents submit bids for all hours in the trading horizon, and they are 4. allow","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"agents submit bids for all hours in the trading horizon, and they are allowed to update their bids between market clearings."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R002-C003","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Agents are allowed to update their supply bids between market clearings. Scope: Updates to supply bids in rolling-horizon operation. Condition: Between successive market clearings.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.supply"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E014"],"ref":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R002::v141-c-R002-C003","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R002","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E014","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p04-c1r1__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"M. Brolin and H. Pihl agents submit bids for all hours in the trading horizon, and they are 4. allow","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"agents submit bids for all hours in the trading horizon, and they are allowed to update their bids between market clearings."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R002-C004","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Supply bids are submitted once per hour, shortly before the beginning of each delivery-hour. Scope: Supply-bid submission timing under the paper's assumed hourly trading periods. Condition: The described schedule assumes 1 h time-periods; the design permits longer or shorter periods.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.supply"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E012","v141-b-g01-E013"],"ref":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R002::v141-c-R002-C004","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R002","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E012","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p03-c2r3__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"4.1.3. Rolling time-horizon a- Energy is traded for discrete time-periods, and the time-periodn- len","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Energy is traded for discrete time-periods, and the time-period length is the same for all energy carriers. Energy in different time-periods are traded as different commodities, and agents submit separate bids for separate time-periods. For clarity, we will here assume that the time-period length is 1 h. However, the time-period length could be both longer and shorter."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E013","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p03-c2r3__v141-a-M01-settlement","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"4.1.3. Rolling time-horizon a- Energy is traded for discrete time-periods, and the time-periodn- len","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"In order to minimize forecast errors, bid submission and market clearing take place as close to the delivery-hour as possible. Therefore, bids are submitted and the market is cleared once per hour, shortly before the beginning of each delivery-hour. However, for the market to be able to accommodate dependencies over longer periods of time, each market clearing also includes a range of future hours. The full range of hours included in a market clearing is referred to as the trading horizon. The first hour in the trading horizon (the upcoming delivery-hour) is referred to as the binding hour, and subsequent hours are referred to as advisory hours. As the names indicate, the market results for the binding hour are final, whereas the results for the advisory hours will be updated in subsequent market clearings."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R002-C005","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Agents may submit multiple supply bids with different quantities and valuations to construct a step-function curve without using bid dependencies. Scope: Permitted construction of supply bid curves. Condition: When constructing a step-function bid curve.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.supply"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E020"],"ref":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R002::v141-c-R002-C005","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R002","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E020","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p04-c1r3__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"GE-dependencies: The sum of the accepted quantity from the bids qb • should be greater than or equal","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"Note that agents can construct some bid combinations without the need to use bid dependencies. For example, step-function bid curves can be built by simply submitting multiple bids with different quantities and valuations."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R002-C006","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Agents cannot submit indivisible supply bids that must be either fully accepted or rejected entirely. Scope: Supply-bid admissibility in the proposed market design.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.supply"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E22"],"ref":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R002::v141-c-R002-C006","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R002","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E22","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p08-c1r4__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":"6.1. The indivisibility issue","anchor_text":"producer may have a minimum load requirement such that it has to either be turned oﬀor operate above","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"exception"},"source_text":"As described in 4.2, the market optimization problem is linear and no integer variables are introduced. This means that there is no possibility for agents to submit indivisible bids, i.e. bids that should be either fully accepted or not accepted at all."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R002-C007","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Supply bids in one hour cannot be conditioned on the outcomes of another hour within the same market clearing. Scope: Supply bids for different hours within one market clearing. Condition: Conditioning a bid in one hour on another hour's outcome within the same clearing.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.supply"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E25"],"ref":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R002::v141-c-R002-C007","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R002","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E25","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p08-c2r4__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":"6.3. Multiple energy carriers and flexibility instruments","anchor_text":"to Even though the proposed ﬂexibility instruments provide a vast list le of options and possibiliti","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"exception"},"source_text":"Even though the proposed flexibility instruments provide a vast list of options and possibilities, there are limitations in what they can represent. For example, since agents cannot submit indivisible bids, the possibility for a market participant to completely switch between electricity and DH cannot be ensured, i.e. it cannot be ensured that only one of these options exclusively will be cleared. Another limitation is the difficulty to construct bids for energy storage that takes full advantage of the flexibility offered by such assets. Although it is possible to construct bids and bid dependencies that represent a specific charge and discharge cycle, it is difficult to fully capture all possibilities and constraints of a typical energy storage. Accurately capturing all possible charge and discharge possibilities over a trading horizon would require a very large number of bids and bid dependencies. Further, the available capacity for hours further out in the horizon depends on the amount cleared in prior hours. However, it is not possible to condition the bids in one hour on the outcomes of another hour within the same market clearing."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C003","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Submitted supply bids provide inputs to local market clearing. Scope: Supply-and-demand inputs to the local multi-energy-carrier auction.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.supply","clearing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E006","v141-b-g01-E022"],"ref":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C003","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R003","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E006","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p03-c1r4__v141-a-M01-participation","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"the local market and other surrounding energy systems. A retailer uptherefore does not represent a p","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The local market clearing function is matching the submitted supply and demand bids, taking into account aspects such as grid constraints. The clearing function is operated by a market operator, which is responsible for the continuous operation of the local market and its supporting functions, and should therefore preferably be financially independent from the owners of the market participants."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E022","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p04-c2r1__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Electrical Power and Energy Systems 118 (2020) 105739 re 4.2. Market clearing and pricing re This se","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"This section provides a mathematical description of the market clearing mechanism, including all the main ingredients discussed in Section 4.1. The market clearing is based on mathematical optimization, where the objective is to maximize the sum of consumer and producer surplus. The problem is kept linear, which means that it can be solved efficiently using available linear programming (LP) software. Input to the market clearing problem consists of bids and bid dependencies, and outputs are the cleared bid quantities and market prices."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C004","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"The offered quantity submitted in a supply bid limits the quantity cleared from that bid: clearing cannot exceed its bid quantity. Scope: The cleared quantity of each supply bid in the local auction.","expression":"0 \\leqslant y_b \\leqslant q_b, \\quad \\forall b \\in B.","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.supply","clearing.local"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R003-X001"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R003-T001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E001","v141-b-g01-E024"],"ref":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C004","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R003","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E001","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p02-c1r1__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":2,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"M. Brolin and H. Pihl Nomenclature L0 Ll Algebraic symbols vb qb B , b set and index of bids Q D , d","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"B, b set and index of bids; D, d set and index of demand bids, D ⊂ B; S, s set and index of supply bids, S ⊂ B; R, r set and index of bid dependencies; R^X set of bid dependencies of type X, R^X ⊂ R; T, t set and index of time steps; E, e set and index of energy carriers; L, l set and index of pricing locations."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E024","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p04-c2r2__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"a 4.2.1. Objective and bid dependencies m The objective for the optimization problem is to maximize ","equation_id":"(2)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The amount to clear from each bid should be non-negative and cannot exceed the bid quantity: 0 \\leqslant y_b \\leqslant q_b, \\quad \\forall b \\in B. \\tag{2}"}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C008","kind":"logical","role":"core","statement":"Receipt of supply submissions forms part of the joint all-bids-received condition under which the operator clears the local market. Scope: The centralized two-sided auction's joint all-bids receipt condition. Condition: All bids for the auction have been received, encompassing both supply and demand submissions.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local","bidding.supply"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E006","v141-b-g01-E007"],"ref":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C008","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R003","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E006","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p03-c1r4__v141-a-M01-participation","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"the local market and other surrounding energy systems. A retailer uptherefore does not represent a p","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The local market clearing function is matching the submitted supply and demand bids, taking into account aspects such as grid constraints. The clearing function is operated by a market operator, which is responsible for the continuous operation of the local market and its supporting functions, and should therefore preferably be financially independent from the owners of the market participants."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E007","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p03-c2r1__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Electrical Power and Energy Systems 118 (2020) 105739 of 4.1. Main ingredients s- se 4.1.1. Centrali","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Like many wholesale electricity markets, the proposed market is based on a centralized two-sided auction format. It is a centralized auction in the sense that all agents submit bids to a central market operator, at a specific time and in accordance with a standardized bid format. Once all bids have been received, the market operator clears the market, meaning that it identifies which bids should be accepted, based on the information contained in the bids. The market operator informs each agent whether or not their bids cleared."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R004-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Supply submissions provide bid inputs to the welfare-maximizing market-clearing optimization. Scope: Market-clearing optimization of the proposed local multi-energy-carrier auction.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.supply","clearing.social_welfare"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E022","v141-b-g01-E023"],"ref":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R004::v141-c-R004-C002","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R004","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E022","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p04-c2r1__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Electrical Power and Energy Systems 118 (2020) 105739 re 4.2. Market clearing and pricing re This se","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"This section provides a mathematical description of the market clearing mechanism, including all the main ingredients discussed in Section 4.1. The market clearing is based on mathematical optimization, where the objective is to maximize the sum of consumer and producer surplus. The problem is kept linear, which means that it can be solved efficiently using available linear programming (LP) software. Input to the market clearing problem consists of bids and bid dependencies, and outputs are the cleared bid quantities and market prices."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E023","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p04-c2r2__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"a 4.2.1. Objective and bid dependencies m The objective for the optimization problem is to maximize ","equation_id":"(1)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The objective for the optimization problem is to maximize consumer and producer surplus, i.e. the difference between the sum of the valuations of all cleared demand bids and the sum of the valuations of all cleared supply bids. The optimization variables are y_b, denoting the amount to clear from each bid. \\max_{y_b} \\left[ \\sum_{b \\in D} v_b \\cdot y_b - \\sum_{b \\in S} v_b \\cdot y_b \\right] \\tag{1}"}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R005-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Supply bids are submitted to the central market operator at a specific time and in accordance with a standardized bid format. Scope: Scheduled bid submission in the centralized two-sided local auction.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.supply","coordination.local_operator"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E007","v141-b-g01-E015"],"ref":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C002","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R005","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E007","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p03-c2r1__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Electrical Power and Energy Systems 118 (2020) 105739 of 4.1. Main ingredients s- se 4.1.1. Centrali","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Like many wholesale electricity markets, the proposed market is based on a centralized two-sided auction format. It is a centralized auction in the sense that all agents submit bids to a central market operator, at a specific time and in accordance with a standardized bid format. Once all bids have been received, the market operator clears the market, meaning that it identifies which bids should be accepted, based on the information contained in the bids. The market operator informs each agent whether or not their bids cleared."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E015","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p04-c1r2__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"energy will be injected or withdrawn). In addition, each bid states a 4. single quantity (in kWh) an","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"In the proposed market design, each individual bid has a very simple structure. Each bid contains basic information about what the bid is for (i.e. it specifies an energy carrier, a delivery-hour, whether it is a supply or demand bid, and the location on the network where the energy will be injected or withdrawn). In addition, each bid states a single quantity (in kWh) and a single valuation (in €/kWh)."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R007-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The local clearing price equals the valuation contained in the highest-valued accepted supply bid when that bid is marginal. Scope: Marginal-bid price determination in the local auction. Condition: There are no network constraints or bid dependencies, and the highest-valued accepted supply bid is marginal.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.supply","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R007-x-lambda"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R007-theta-v"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E015","v141-b-g01-E042"],"ref":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R007::v141-c-R007-C002","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R007","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E015","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p04-c1r2__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"energy will be injected or withdrawn). In addition, each bid states a 4. single quantity (in kWh) an","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"In the proposed market design, each individual bid has a very simple structure. Each bid contains basic information about what the bid is for (i.e. it specifies an energy carrier, a delivery-hour, whether it is a supply or demand bid, and the location on the network where the energy will be injected or withdrawn). In addition, each bid states a single quantity (in kWh) and a single valuation (in €/kWh)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E042","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p05-c2r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"al ( y y), j o- have preferred to trade (they are out-of-the-money). The market clearing prices can ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"In a simple case where there are no network constraints and no bid dependencies, the shadow price for a power balance constraint equals the valuation of the highest-valued accepted supply bid, or the highest-valued rejected demand bid, depending on which is marginal. Therefore, the shadow prices are market clearing in this simple case."}]}],"variables":[{"variable_id":"v141-c-R003-X001","symbol":"y_b","meaning":"Amount cleared from bid b, in kWh; shorthand for y_{b,t,e,l} when time, energy-carrier and pricing-location indices are not needed. It is the optimization variable of the local clearing.","kind":"operational","domain":"Real-valued; 0 ≤ y_b ≤ q_b for every bid b ∈ B (Eq. 2)","unit":"kWh","indices":["b"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E002","v141-b-g01-E023","v141-b-g01-E024"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R003","declaration_ref":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-X001"},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R007-x-lambda","symbol":"λ_{t,e,l}","meaning":"Local market clearing price for time-period t, energy carrier e and pricing location l, determined by the market operator and compatible with the cleared-bid solution; source states it can be obtained from the shadow prices of the power-balance constraints (12).","kind":"operational","domain":"price in currency/kWh; the supplied text does not state a sign or numeric interval for λ_{t,e,l}","unit":"currency/kWh (currency glyph omitted in supplied text layer for λ)","indices":["t","e","l"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E002","v141-b-g01-E040","v141-b-g01-E041"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R007","declaration_ref":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R007::x::v141-c-R007-x-lambda"}],"parameters":[{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R003-T001","symbol":"q_b","meaning":"Bid quantity in kWh; upper bound on the amount cleared from bid b.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"kWh","indices":["b"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E002","v141-b-g01-E024"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R003","declaration_ref":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-T001"},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R007-theta-v","symbol":"v_{b,t,e,l}","meaning":"Valuation stated in bid b for delivery time-period t, energy carrier e and pricing location l; used to identify the marginal bid valuation in the no-network/no-dependency special case.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"€/kWh","indices":["b","t","e","l"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E002","v141-b-g01-E015","v141-b-g01-E042"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R007","declaration_ref":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R007::theta::v141-c-R007-theta-v"}]}],"source_definitions":[{"unit_id":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-a-M01::bidding.supply","stage":"L3","subtype":"supply_quantity_valuation_submission","projection_status":"clear","target_definition":"The supplier submits a standardized offer specifying the energy-carrying variety, delivery period, supply identifier, and injection location, and declares a single supply quantity q_b and unit valuation v_b as auction clearing input.","form_kind":"procedural","identity_fields":["Object: supply-side energy offer","Core operation: submit available quantity and unit valuation to the market operator","Output: offer record with commodity, period, location, and supply-direction identifiers"],"variation_fields":["Follows the period-by-period declaration arrangement of the complete trading window, and does not require every hourly offer to be a supply offer","The example submits before each hourly delivery, other period lengths are allowed, and updates may be made between adjacent clearings","Multiple offers with different quantities and valuations can construct a step supply curve without using offer dependencies","Indivisible offers are prohibited, and offer conditions may not be set within the same clearing according to another hour's result"],"constraint_refs":["48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R002::v141-c-R002-C001","48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R002::v141-c-R002-C002","48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R002::v141-c-R002-C003","48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R002::v141-c-R002-C005","48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R002::v141-c-R002-C006","48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R002::v141-c-R002-C007","48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C002"],"paper_id":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","function":"bidding.supply","template_code":"DA"}],"source_variants":[{"unit_id":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-a-M01::bidding.supply","retained_variants":["The standardized offer specifies the energy-carrying variety, delivery period, supply identifier, and injection location, and submits a single supply quantity q_b and unit valuation v_b.","Declarations are made period by period within the complete trading window, and not every hour is required to be a supply offer; the example submits before each hourly delivery, other period lengths may be used, and updates may be made between adjacent clearings.","Multiple offers with different quantities and prices can construct a step supply curve without offer dependencies; indivisible offers and conditions set within the same clearing based on another hour's clearing result are prohibited."],"evidence_refs":["48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-a-M01::bidding.supply::projection"]}],"functional":{"is_child":true,"subdivision_pending":false,"baseline_parent_id":"COMP-0925dd10f543dd2a","baseline_parent_code":"BID014","secondary_class":"SC-L3-bb9e7457976d4f9a","category":{"id":"SC-L3-bb9e7457976d4f9a","stage":"L3","label_zh":"Multi-energy-carrying commodity supply declaration","definition_zh":"The supplier submits supply quantity and price or unit valuation for energy-carrying commodities not limited to electricity, retaining commodity identification and delivery conditions as commodity supply-side clearing input.","main_identity_axes":["Energy-commodity supplier","Supply of energy-carrying commodities not limited to electricity","Declare supply quantity and economic valuation to the market"],"inclusion_criteria":["The atomic rule covers multi-energy-carrying or non-electric energy commodities and cannot be fully limited to electricity sales.","Submit the supply quantity and price or unit valuation of the corresponding commodity for market acceptance or clearing.","The commodity, delivery location, and period are identified according to the source, without presupposing cross-commodity coupling."],"exclusion_criteria":["An electricity-selling intention declaration whose economic object is explicitly only electricity.","Only generation or net supply statistics are reported.","Regulation-service offers relative to a baseline, exemption requirements, or pure energy-purchase requests."],"supporting_unit_ids":["48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-a-M01::bidding.supply"],"status":"agent_defined_structurally_validated"},"definition":{"definition_zh":"The supplier submits the supply quantity and unit valuation according to the energy-carrying commodity identifier, forming an energy-commodity auction input not limited to electricity.","identity_fields":["Submitter: energy-commodity supplier","Object: supply quantity and valuation identified by energy-carrying variety","Function: provide supply-side clearing input for the commodity"],"member_unit_ids":["48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-a-M01::bidding.supply"]}},"canonical_pointer":"/nodes/7"});
